-- title:
--   Piecewise constant lifts on the line
-- statement:
--   For a finite set $D\subset\mathbb Z$, a mesh $h>0$ and $f:D\to E$ with values in an additive monoid, the grid line lift is
--   $$
--   \mathrm{gridLine}(D,h,f)(x)=\sum_{i\in D}\mathbf 1_{[hi,h(i+1))}(x)\,f(i).
--   $$
--   It is the step function equal to $f(i)$ on the cell $[hi,h(i+1))$ and $0$ outside the cells of $D$. Sums over the grid become integrals of the lift. For instance $\int\mathrm{gridLine}(D,h,f)=h\sum_if(i)$ for real-valued $f$.
-- source:
